<title>FRANCE: CNP sees four to five pct 1997 net profit growth.</title>
<headline>CNP sees four to five pct 1997 net profit growth.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caisse Nationale de Prevoyance (CNP) expects an increase of four to five percent in 1997 net profit from 1.57 billion francs in 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;As far as our net result is concerned, we are quite certain that we will do better than in 1996. We are expecting a rise of four to five percent,&quot; chairman Pierre Darnis told a news conference.</p>
<p>But he added that the rise in sales would be significantly lower than the 19 percent rise to over 100 billion francs of 1996.</p>
</text>
